# Optional — enables OpenAI Realtime / GPT / TTS on the server
# Get your key at: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-api-key-here

# Optional — force browser fallback pipeline (same as local Demo Mode)
# Set to "true" on Vercel if you want Demo Mode behavior even with OPENAI_API_KEY set
# VOICE_FORCE_FALLBACK=true

# Without a valid OPENAI_API_KEY, the app automatically uses:
# - Local built-in conversation engine (client-side in Demo Mode)
# - Browser SpeechRecognition (STT)
# - Server cloud TTS for Tamil (Microsoft Pallavi voice — same on all devices)
# - Browser speechSynthesis only as last-resort fallback

# --- Local development ---
# cp .env.example .env.local
# Leave OPENAI_API_KEY blank (or unset) for free Demo Mode locally

# --- Vercel deployment ---
# 1. Push repo to GitHub and import at https://vercel.com/new
# 2. Project Settings → Environment Variables:
#    - OPENAI_API_KEY (optional) — omit for free Demo Mode on production
#    - VOICE_FORCE_FALLBACK=true (optional) — match local Demo Mode on Vercel
# 3. Disable Deployment Protection for public demos:
#    Project Settings → Deployment Protection → turn OFF for Production
# 4. Deploy (framework: Next.js, build: npm run build)
#
# Vercel note: server filesystem is read-only. Voice appointments, dashboard
# metrics, and notifications are stored in each visitor's browser (localStorage).
# Data on vercel.app does NOT sync with localhost — same browser + same URL only.

# --- Scripts only (not used by the app at runtime) ---
# TEST_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/chat
